From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:28:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d: the winemetal facade under mtld3d's conventions (its
 audit and clippy clean)

The M2a review's finding that mtld3d's own audit failed on the facade:
doc blocks in their shape, module visibility instead of pub(crate),
FxHashMap, LazyLock where the initializer is static, metal.rs for
metal/mod.rs, Clone/Copy derives only where used (the inventory
recorded), the facade builds' dead code gated by cfg instead of one
crate-wide allow, the vendored snmalloc-sys skipped by the audit as
third-party. Two accepted exception classes for the facade's objc2
mirror (too_many_arguments on objc2's own method signatures,
NSString::from_str), named in CONVENTIONS.md. The guest's pool test
commits its 1000 buffers: a queue holds at most 64 uncompleted ones,
and the host's Metal blocks its executor on the 65th.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
